    {
      "rank": 8,
      "row_id": 302269,
      "chunk_id": "acf470c530a4_0",
      "doc_id": "acf470c530a4",
      "text": "Unlocked US version: Works on Verizon but not easily. Bought the A51 unlocked US version. Went to a Verizon store and got a new SIM card. The phone was activated but cannot make call/texts or receive calls/texts. It can get data though. The \"Mobile Voice Network Type\" shows \"LTE\" when it should show \"CDMA 1xrtt\". This is what prevents it from being able to use calls/texts on the phone. I tried another sim card from my Samsung Galaxy S9 and it did the exact same thing. Wrong type of data is being read by the phone for the voice calling. Update: After being in good service areas for the Verizon network for about 2 days with multiple factory resets, the phone has been working fully on the Verizon network now. Not sure what happened but it has been functional for 1 month now.",
      "score": 0.033204487698552144,
      "brand": "Samsung",
      "model": "Galaxy A51",
      "rating": 3,
